@startuml
title Order path — from client to committed fill
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam SequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam SequenceParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam SequenceBoxBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam SequenceBoxBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

actor Client
participant "API server" as API
participant "Validator node" as Node
participant "HyperBFT" as BFT
participant "Order book" as OB
participant "Clearinghouse" as CH

Client -> API : signed action (nonce, EIP-712)
API -> Node : forward
Node -> BFT : gossip into round
BFT -> BFT : quorum of 2/3 stake signs
note right of BFT
  Actions inside the block are sorted:
  1. no GTC/IOC order
  2. cancels
  3. at least one GTC/IOC
  proposer order applies within each class
end note
BFT -> OB : committed, ordered actions
OB -> CH : margin check on placement
CH --> OB : accept or reject
OB -> OB : match at price-time priority
OB -> CH : margin check for the resting side\nat each match
CH -> CH : update positions and balances
CH --> API : execution response
API --> Client : committed result (median 0.2 s)
@enduml
